So its time complexity is O(n^2) and space complexity is O(1).SO it is not recommended at that to use bubble sort.

Why its name is bubble sort?
Bubble Sort is called Bubble Sort because the largest elements repeatedly "bubble"/move toward the end of the array through adjacent swaps.


How to make bubble sort better?
If on any iteration,no swapping is happening,its mean array is already sorted ,so we dont need extra iterations,for example [9,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],in this array,in first iteration,  first element will be placed at last, after that no need of iterations because array is already sorted.So we should stop it.

Solution:
let arr=[9,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8];
  let n=arr.length;
for (let i=0;i<n-1;i++){
  let isSwapped=false
   for (let j=0;j<n-1-i;j++){
     if (arr[j]>arr[j+1]){
     let temp=arr[j]
     arr[j]=arr[j+1]
     arr[j+1]=temp
       isSwapped=true
   }}
  if (!isSwapped) break;
}
